/* ==================================================================
   S C O P ' D
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Black Ops II  //  Cronus Zen / GPC                     v5.6
   SNIPER BUILD  -  OFFLINE / BOT LOBBY / CAMPAIGN
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   MENU        : hold L2 + tap OPTIONS
   MASTER KILL : hold L2 + tap SHARE
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.6 - INFADE STAGGER FIX (this still didn't do it in-game)

   v5.5's "hold FIRE+RELOAD together, then spam SWAP" was simultaneous
   - both buttons landing on the same tick. Confirmed against how the
   trick is actually taught: RELOAD goes down first and is held on
   its own for a beat, THEN FIRE joins while RELOAD stays held, and
   only once both are held do you spam SWAP. Simultaneous press never
   lets a real reload state start, so there was nothing for the SWAP
   spam to interrupt/loop - which is exactly "doesn't do it."

   The RELOAD-alone lead before FIRE joins is FADE_LEAD_MS (40ms) -
   a fixed constant, NOT a new CAN TUNE field. First attempt added it
   as a 7th CAN TUNE option, which grew every option-metadata array by
   one element; on this compiler each array element is its own VM
   stack slot, and that pushed the build 3 slots past the 1024-slot
   limit (GPC4011). Reverted to a plain #define instead - costs zero
   stack slots, at the price of not being tunable in-menu. FADE HOLD
   is now the delay after FIRE joins (not from t=0) before the SWAP
   spam starts; FADE GAP unchanged. If it still doesn't catch, FADE
   HOLD/GAP are the only two left to nudge on CAN TUNE - FADE_LEAD_MS
   itself would need a script edit.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.5 - INFADE MECHANIC CORRECTED

   v5.4 guessed at an ADS-transition-timing mechanic. That's not how
   this actually works - corrected based on the real technique: fire
   at least one round first (on you, before triggering this - the
   script has no way to know your clip state), then hold FIRE and
   RELOAD together, and while both stay held, rapidly spam SWAP -
   that loops the reload sound and animation without spending real
   ammo. Rebuilt ts_build()'s INFADE section around that: FIRE+RELOAD
   held for the whole sequence, SWAP spammed inside that hold instead
   of a separate ADS/FIRE cycle.

   This also means BTN_ADS is untouched again - FIRE is now the only
   button INFADE adds to the "never touched by any other trick" list,
   not ADS. FADE HOLD is the delay before the spam starts (let RELOAD
   actually register); FADE GAP is spacing between SWAP taps during
   the spam - tightened its default from 80ms to 20ms to match "rapid
   spam," since 80 was sized for the old cycle-based design, not this
   one.

   INFADENAC's cancel changed from RELOAD to AXE - pairing it with
   RELOAD was redundant now that the fade itself already holds
   RELOAD throughout.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.4 - INFINITE FADE

   New mechanic, and the one deliberate exception to a rule that's
   held since early in this project: every other trick never touches
   FIRE or ADS. Infade IS an ADS/FIRE rhythm - firing while still
   mid-transition into the scope, before it settles, chained back to
   back - so there's no way to build it without breaking that rule
   on purpose, scoped to just this.

   INFADE REPS: new 9th field on custom slots (SLOT EDIT), 0-6, mixes
   with the existing PRE/CAN/FIN fields on any slot. New INFADE
   family in the library - INFADE (bare), INFADEYY, INFADENAC,
   INFADEMEL - pairing the fade cycling with a plain cancel or a
   NAC-shaped one, as asked. Fade cycles run first, whatever cancel/
   finish is attached lands after.

   FADE HOLD / FADE GAP on CAN TUNE, tunable from the start rather
   than guessed - no published BO2 data exists for the transition
   window's real length, and by every account this is one of the
   hardest tricks to land even by hand. Starting values are order-of-
   magnitude guesses, not measured; expect to actually dial these in.

   Slot storage grew a field (8 -> 9), which meant repacking how
   slots are saved - old saved slot data doesn't translate to the new
   layout, so this is a clean settings reset (MAGIC bumped 94 -> 95),
   same call as the v4.0 layout change. Custom slots A-D go back to
   their SLOTDEF defaults; everything else (binds, timing, CAN TUNE)
   goes back to defaults too and needs reconfiguring.

   Also: the move library grew from 29 to 33 entries, which meant
   custom slots had to shift from mac 30-33 to mac 34-37 to avoid
   colliding with the new INFADE moves - caught and fixed everywhere
   that boundary was hardcoded (ts_load, the bind browser, the
   timeline header, the bind-summary row).
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.3 - SPIN HOLDS THROUGH CANCEL OVERRUN

   Real bug, confirmed by tracing the actual timing model: the spin
   window's duration is calibrated purely from the chosen spin amount
   (CALIBRATE depends on that staying exact) and has zero awareness
   of how long PRE+CANCEL take to play out. For short sequences
   that's invisible - CANCEL always finishes well inside the spin.
   For long ones - MONSTR's SPRINT+JUMP pre plus three chained
   cancels is the worst case in the library - CANCEL can genuinely
   outrun a short spin pick, and the camera stops dead while cancel
   presses keep firing. That's what "everything happens after the
   spin" was.

   Fix: ts_build() now tracks sp_hold, the later of the spin's
   calibrated end or the cancel chain's actual end. spin_pow() clamps
   its ramp position at 100% once past the calibrated duration, so
   the extended portion holds at the already-tapered tail power
   instead of extrapolating the ramp - the calibrated rotation amount
   is completely unchanged, this only stops the stick going idle
   early. FINISH is deliberately excluded - a PRONE+MELEE landing
   (MONSTR) is meant to read as the camera having already settled,
   not still spinning.

   Also added a full button-macro reference for all 29 library moves,
   generated straight from MOVEDEF - see SCOPD_trickshot_macros.md.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.2 - LED: FOUND THE REAL BUG. CANCEL TIMING: MADE TUNABLE
   INSTEAD OF GUESSED AGAIN

   The LED "flashing" wasn't a frequency problem - v5.1's 300ms
   throttle didn't fix it because that was never the real cause.
   Checked the actual Cronus docs this time: their own example code
   shows set_ps4_lbar(0,255,0) is RED, not set_ps4_lbar(255,0,0) -
   the channel order is B,R,G, not R,G,B. That was a confirmed,
   documented bug (https://gpc.cronusmax.com/functions-and-commands/
   controller-functions/leds), not a guess. Also switched from a
   periodic reassert to purely event-driven: the LED is only set once
   at boot and again exactly when master_off changes, never on a
   timer, so it can't be caught fighting anything on a cycle.

   Cancel timing: did real research this time - confirmed again there
   is no published BO2 frame data anywhere, for anyone, and confirmed
   I have no way to watch footage and extract timing from it even if
   it existed. Two straight guesses (v5.0's fixed constants, v5.1's
   TAP-scaled multipliers) both came back wrong in opposite
   directions. Rather than guess a third time, RLD MULT / AXE MULT /
   MEL MULT are now on their own page - CAN TUNE - adjustable while
   actually watching it happen in a match, plus a FIRE TEST action
   that fires a RELOAD-cancel 360 without leaving the menu. Starting
   values are unchanged from v5.1 (x3 / x2 / +10) - nudge from there
   with real feedback instead of another blind number from me.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.1 - LED FIX, CANCEL TIMING TAKE TWO

   LED was flashing on idle: calling set_rgb/set_ps4_lbar every single
   main-loop tick (far faster than 33ms) was likely flooding the LED
   update instead of holding it steady. Throttled to once every
   ~300ms. Also switched from pink to solid red while armed, off
   while unarmed, per request - and if the color comes out wrong
   rather than flashing, some Zen firmware ships set_ps4_lbar in BRG
   channel order instead of RGB; that's a firmware thing, not this
   script, and the fix is swapping argument order.

   Cancel timing, second attempt: the v5.0 fixed constants (RELOAD
   260ms, AXE/TAC 170ms, MELEE 110ms) were a blind guess with nothing
   to validate them against, and they guessed wrong - reported as
   both still not showing the animation AND noticeably slower overall.
   Rather than guess a third set of fixed numbers with the same
   problem, cancel_hold() now scales off TAP instead of using its own
   disconnected constants (RELOAD x3, AXE/TAC x2, MELEE +10), so
   there's one dial - TAP, already on TS TIMING - that moves all of
   them together if this still isn't right. Defaults are much shorter
   than v5.0's guess (84/56/38ms at the default TAP of 28 vs the
   previous 260/170/110).
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v5.0 - TRICKSHOT REWORK: FAMILIES, DECOUPLED SPIN, SWITCH, AUTO
   CANCEL TIMING

   Pages reordered: TRICKSHOT, TS BINDS, TS TIMING, CALIBRATE, TS
   BINDS+, SLOT EDIT, then everything else in its old relative order.
   PG_SLOT moved in lockstep with SLOT EDIT's new position - it has
   to, or the v10 silent-save bug comes straight back.

   Pink on the Zen's own LED and the DS4 lightbar, set every tick
   (set_rgb + set_ps4_lbar) so the console can't override it back.

   RELOAD/AXE/MELEE/TAC cancels no longer share the plain TAP value
   for their trigger press - cancel_hold() gives each its own
   reasoned hold time (RELOAD 260ms, AXE/TAC 170ms, MELEE 110ms) so
   the animation actually starts before the cancel swap fires. BO2
   has no published frame data for this, so these are tuned defaults,
   not measured - report back if reload still feels early or late.

   The trickshot library is a full rebuild. SPIN is no longer baked
   into a trick - it's chosen when you bind it - so one "AXE" move
   now covers every spin amount instead of needing AXE360/540/720/
   1080 as four separate slots. 29 moves across 7 families (BASICS,
   CANCELS, COMBOS, NAC, SWAPS, MOVEMENT, OTHER) plus SLOTS as an 8th
   browsable group for the custom A-D slots. TS BINDS and TS BINDS+
   now open a 3-screen picker on OK - family, then trick, then spin -
   instead of cycling a flat 45-item list.

   New per-bind SWITCH flag, set on the spin screen (UP/DOWN toggles
   it): flips the spin direction at the midpoint instead of holding
   one direction the whole way, for tricks that spin one way then the
   other. Doesn't touch button choreography, only which way the stick
   is pushed past 50% through the spin window.

   NAC family (Money/Titty/Reload/Hybrid/Selfire NAC) and SWAPS
   additions (Insta-Swap, Knife Flip) are new. Several collapse to
   the same underlying shape as an existing cancel type (e.g. Titty
   NAC and Hybrid NAC are both a plain swap-timed cancel) - that's a
   real limit of what a fixed button sequence can express, not a bug;
   noted here rather than faked as more distinct than they are.

   MOVEMENT gained NSL, Ladder Stall, Top Spin, Running Man and
   Moonwalk - button-timing only, exactly as asked: these need real
   positioning (a ledge, a ladder, momentum) or a sustained stick hold
   a macro can't provide blind, so what's scripted is only the
   button/timing piece each actually has. Top Spin in particular has
   no real button component - true vertical spin isn't something the
   current spin engine (horizontal only) can do - so it's a bare spin
   with an in-menu note, not a fabricated mechanic.

   Custom slots (SLOT EDIT) are unchanged - still 8 fields, still
   don't have a SWITCH field of their own. Say the word if you want
   that added too.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.6 - DECLASSIFY BOOT, STATUS STRIP IDLE VIEW

   Boot no longer runs the eyes - it's a declassify reveal instead:
   CLEARANCE/GRANTED, a redacted OPERATOR ID that never resolves (not
   real data, just texture), the brand line, then LOADING hands off
   to the same progress bar that already ran from t=2600. Same total
   boot budget as before (3.6s), nothing about the timing changed.

   New IDLE VIEW option on DISPLAY (EYES / STATUS, default EYES - no
   existing save changes behavior on its own). STATUS shows a
   read-only status strip instead of the eyes: TRICKSHOT, QUICKSCOPE,
   STEAL EMBLEM (ARMED instead of ON, since that one fires an actual
   input sequence), and a HOLD L2+OPTIONS hint at the bottom. Nothing
   on it is editable - it's a status display, not a menu page; you
   still open the real config the same way as always.

   The eyes - blink curve, iris drift, tear physics, EYE BLINK / EYE
   LOOK / TEAR - are untouched and still the default. This adds a
   second view, it doesn't replace the first.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.5 - 540/720 TIERS FOR AXE/RLD/MEL/TEMPER/BARREL

   YY180, YY1080, YYY720, YY2360, YY2720, JMPYY, DRPMEL, YY3360,
   YY3720, RUN1080 removed to make room (10 slots - none of them were
   in any default bind, checked before touching anything). In their
   place: AXE540/AXE720, RLD540/RLD720, MEL540/MEL720, TMP540/TMP720,
   BAR540/BAR720 - the missing middle tiers between each trick's 360
   version and its v4.4 1080 version. Every family (AXE/RLD/MEL/TMP/
   BAR) now has 360, 540, 720, and 1080 all available.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.4 - FIVE NEW 1080 TRICKS

   RUNJMP, RUN720, DIV360, DIV720, DIVYY (dive/run tricks) removed to
   make room. In their place: AXE1080, RLD1080, MEL1080, TMP1080 (the
   TEMPER jump+YY+swap-finish shape at 1080 instead of 360), BAR1080
   (BARREL's swap-pre+YY shape at 1080). Same fields as their 360
   counterparts, SPIN bumped to the 1080 enum value. No other slot
   moved - default binds only ever pointed at 2/4/6/8/16/19/22/29,
   none of which were touched.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.3 - PAGE COUNTER FIX, XTRA DOWN, TS AUTO

   Page header was showing "14/12": the "/N" total was never a real
   number, it was two hardcoded characters '1' and '2' left over from
   when there were 12 pages. Both halves of the counter render off
   the real page numbers now.

   STEAL EMBLEM gained XTRA DOWN (0-6, default 4): extra DOWN presses
   tacked onto the base 2 at the end of the sequence. This needed the
   macro to stop being a combo - combos can't loop or branch, and a
   runtime-variable repeat count needs both - so it's now a small
   tick-driven sequencer (se_start/se_run) instead, same pattern the
   trickshot engine already uses for its own windows.

   SYSTEM gained TS AUTO: loads the tested TS TIMING baseline (TAP
   28, GAP 24, STAGE 7, LEAD 0, PRE 8, FIN 4, TAIL 6) in one press
   instead of resetting seven lines by hand with TRIANGLE. It's the
   documented starting point, not a live calibration - CALIBRATE's
   FIRE TEST / APPLY FIX / TUNE GAP is still what actually tunes it
   to your setup from there.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.2 - STEAL EMBLEM TAB

   New page, nothing else touched. STEAL EMBLEM is a fixed menu-
   navigation sequence for the Barracks emblem-copy glitch - X,
   Circle x3, X, X, Down x2 - fired by a bindable trigger (L3/R3/L1/
   R1) while ENABLE is on, with its own TAP/GAP timing since a menu's
   input window behaves nothing like a match's. FIRE TEST runs it
   once from the menu for tuning. It's a straight combo, not the
   trickshot sequencer - the sequence is fixed length and strictly
   serial, nothing to overlap.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.1 - SLOT EDIT ACTUALLY SAVES NOW

   PG_SLOT (the page id slot_sync() gates on) was defined as 4, which
   is CALIBRATE - SLOT EDIT is page 3. slot_sync() only ever runs
   "if(m_page == PG_SLOT)", so with the wrong id it silently did
   nothing the entire time you were on the real SLOT EDIT page: your
   PRE 1 / PRE 2 / CANCEL 1-4 / SPIN / FINISH edits changed the number
   on screen (that's just oval[]) but never touched ts_slot[], so
   firing SLOTA-D always played whatever ts_slot[] already held, and
   SAVE ALL / CIRCLE-to-exit wrote that same untouched data back out.
   Selecting a different slot in EDIT SLOT didn't reload its fields
   either, for the same reason. One-line fix: PG_SLOT = 3.

   Also corrected O_SL_CAN3's default (ODEF) to YY, matching SLOTDEF
   A's actual third cancel - it had drifted to NONE, which only ever
   showed up if you pressed TRIANGLE to reset that one line.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v4.0 - SNIPER ONLY, AIM PRECISION REBUILT, FOUR CANCELS

   Every option that wasn't sniping or trickshotting is gone: SNAP
   AIM, SCOPE BAIT, SEMI AUTO (rapid fire + anti-recoil) and HAIR
   TRIGGER are deleted outright, not just hidden. That's 15 pages
   down to 12, and every remaining page earns its place.

   AIM ASSIST is not the same feature anymore. CIRCLE / PULSE /
   STRAFE were stick-wiggle patterns injected on top of your real
   input regardless of whether you were also moving it - which is
   what "tweaking" on small corrections actually was. It's replaced
   by three things that shape YOUR input instead of fighting it:
     CURVE   - precision near centre, speed further out
     SMOOTH  - low-pass filter that kills hand tremor / micro-jitter
     BREATH LINK - both tighten automatically while breath is held
   plus an optional, small, heavily-suppressed MICRO NUDGE for
   anyone who still wants a magnetism-style pull - off by default.

   SLOT EDIT goes to FOUR cancel stages (was three), because there
   was never a real reason it should have had fewer cancels than
   pre-moves and finishers had headroom for. To make room without
   breaking the two-pvar / 3-bit-per-field save packing, FINISH
   drops from two fields to one - with a new composite "PR+MEL"
   value so a PRONE-then-MELEE ending (MONSTR, DRPMEL) still works
   in a single field. Every existing macro re-expresses cleanly in
   the new 8-field shape: 2 PRE, 4 CANCEL, 1 SPIN, 1 FINISH.

   Pages reordered: AIM ASSIST stays 1, then TRICKSHOT (2), TS
   TIMING (3), SLOT EDIT (4), TS BINDS (5), TS BINDS+ (6) - the
   sequencer is now front and centre instead of buried on page 9.
   TURBO MELEE moved from the deleted TRIGGERS page into MOVEMENT,
   which otherwise keeps everything it had.

   OLED: boot and idle no longer print "SCOP'D" or draw the rule
   line under it - idle is eyes only now, always, no more SCOPE /
   BINDS / CYCLE views. That runner-simulation scene, the bind
   preview screen and their support code are gone along with the
   IDLE VIEW option.

   BREAKING: this is enough of a structural change to the save
   format (new fields, deleted fields, different slot packing) that
   trying to migrate every old value field-by-field was more risk
   than it was worth getting quietly wrong. v4.0 resets ALL saved
   settings on first load, once - not just the four custom slots as
   past layout changes have done. Re-tune TS TIMING and re-bind your
   directions after the first boot on this version.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.2 - AIM ASSIST STOPPED FIGHTING SMALL CORRECTIONS

   The assist offset (CIRCLE/PULSE/STRAFE) was being added straight on
   top of the real right-stick value with no regard for whether the
   player was also moving it. A full-power assist vector stacked on a
   tiny manual nudge is what "tweaking" on small aim adjustments was -
   the offset dominated the input instead of assisting it. Superseded
   by the v4.0 aim precision rebuild above.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.1 - EIGHT FIELDS

   v3.0 gave a trickshot four named sections, which fixed the flow but
   allowed exactly ONE cancel. Long shots need more: a running jump
   buys close to a second of airtime and you want two or three cancels
   inside it, spaced differently from the taps inside each one.

   So a trickshot is eight fields now:

       PRE 1     PRE 2     CANCEL 1  CANCEL 2
       CANCEL 3  SPIN      FINISH 1  FINISH 2

   PRE 2 exists mainly for SPRINT + JUMP. Sprint deliberately stays
   held past the point the jump fires, so the jump goes off while you
   are still running - a running jump, which is the higher, longer one
   with room for the extra cancels.

   And GAP split in two. GAP is the rhythm INSIDE one cancel; STAGE is
   the rest between one cancel and the next. One number could not
   express "tight YY, loose spacing between cancels", which is what a
   multi-cancel shot actually needs.

   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v3.0 - SECTIONED TRICKSHOTS

   v2 made the spin parallel but still laid the button presses end to
   end, and it stored a slot as eight loose "steps" - so a jump shot
   was jump, wait, swap, wait, swap, and nothing overlapped except the
   stick. That is what "not smooth" was.

   v3 gives every trickshot four named sections that deliberately
   overlap in time:

       PRE      jump / dive / swap-out / prone / crouch / sprint
       CANCEL   YY / YYY / YYYY / reload / axe / melee / tac
       SPIN     180 .. 1080, off one calibrated SPIN 360ms
       FINISH   prone / melee / swap / crouch / jump / reload

   CANCEL starts PRE x10 INTO the pre-move rather than after it, so
   the YY lands while you are still coming off the jump. FINISH fires
   FIN x10 after whichever of CANCEL and SPIN ends last. The library
   macros are just named presets over those four fields (MOVEDEF[]),
   and the four custom slots compose the same four fields by hand.

   The spin also has an envelope now - whip out, carry, settle - so it
   stops looking like a switch. SPIN RAMP sets the depth, and the
   window is lengthened by exactly the area the envelope gives up, so
   the rotation stays calibrated at every setting.

   NOTHING TOUCHES L2 OR R2. No auto-scope, no auto-fire. The macro
   choreographs the movement and the cancels; you scope and you shoot.

   Every gap is tunable on TS TIMING - see the README.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   GPC NOTES: no local variables - all working vars are top level,
   prefixed by owner. Combos take set_val/wait only, no branching,
   which is exactly why the sequencer lives in a function instead.
   print() takes a data-section address, not a literal; no %d.

   SCREEN BUDGET (128 x 64, small font 7px wide / 8px tall):
     header y 0..11 | rows y 15,25,35,45,55 | labels x 3 (10 chars)
     values x 76 (6 chars) | scrollbar x 121..125
   ================================================================== */


/* ---------------- BUTTON LAYOUT (edit me) ---------------- */
define BTN_FIRE    = PS4_R2;
define BTN_ADS     = PS4_L2;
define BTN_MELEE   = PS4_R3;
define BTN_BREATH  = PS4_L3;     /* sprint, and hold-breath while scoped */
define BTN_JUMP    = PS4_CROSS;
define BTN_CROUCH  = PS4_CIRCLE; /* tap = crouch, hold = prone */
define BTN_RELOAD  = PS4_SQUARE;
define BTN_SWAP    = PS4_TRIANGLE;
define BTN_MENU    = PS4_OPTIONS;
define BTN_MASTER  = PS4_SHARE;
define BTN_TAC     = PS4_L1;
define BTN_LETHAL  = PS4_R1;     /* combat axe for the AXE cancel */

define STK_RX = PS4_RX;
define STK_RY = PS4_RY;
define STK_LX = PS4_LX;
define STK_LY = PS4_LY;

/* ---------------- MENU NAVIGATION ---------------- */
define NAV_UP    = PS4_UP;
define NAV_DOWN  = PS4_DOWN;
define NAV_LEFT  = PS4_LEFT;
define NAV_RIGHT = PS4_RIGHT;
define NAV_PGL   = PS4_L1;
define NAV_PGR   = PS4_R1;
define NAV_OK    = PS4_CROSS;
define NAV_DEF   = PS4_TRIANGLE;
define NAV_EXIT  = PS4_CIRCLE;

/* ---------------- OPTION IDs (also the LBL[] index) ---------------- */
define O_AA_CURVE   = 0;      /* p1  AIM ASSIST */
define O_AA_SMOOTH  = 1;
define O_AA_BLINK   = 2;
define O_AA_NUDGE   = 3;
define O_AA_NPWR    = 4;

define O_TS_ON      = 5;      /* p2  TRICKSHOT */
define O_TS_MOD     = 6;
define O_TS_DIR     = 7;
define O_TS_SPIN    = 8;
define O_TS_RAMP    = 9;      /* whip-and-settle envelope depth */
define O_TS_ABORT   = 10;     /* hand the stick back when you scope */
define O_TS_LOOP    = 11;     /* hold the direction to repeat */

define O_TAP        = 12;     /* p3  TS TIMING */
define O_GAP        = 13;     /* between taps INSIDE one cancel      */
define O_STAGE      = 14;     /* between one cancel and the next     */
define O_LEAD       = 15;
define O_PRE        = 16;     /* pre-move -> cancel overlap          */
define O_FIN        = 17;     /* (cancel|spin) end -> finish, and
                                 within a composite finish            */
define O_TAIL       = 18;

/* p4  SLOT EDIT - these EIGHT must stay consecutive and in field
   order; slot_sync() and ts_load() both walk them as a block. */
define O_SLOT_SEL   = 19;
define O_SL_PRE1    = 20;
define O_SL_PRE2    = 21;
define O_SL_CAN1    = 22;
define O_SL_CAN2    = 23;
define O_SL_CAN3    = 24;
define O_SL_CAN4    = 25;
define O_SL_SPIN    = 26;
define O_SL_FIN     = 27;
define O_SL_INFADE  = 28;     /* 9th slot field - INFADE reps, 0-6, 0=off */

/* p5  CALIBRATE - the spin/timing trainer. CAL TEST runs the chosen
   reference macro and starts a measurement window; CAL RESULT is what
   you tell it you actually got, and CAL APPLY solves for the corrected
   SPIN 360ms from those two numbers. */
define O_CAL_REF    = 29;
define O_CAL_TEST   = 30;
define O_CAL_GOT    = 31;
define O_CAL_APPLY  = 32;
define O_CAL_GAP    = 33;

define O_BIND_U     = 34;     /* p6  TS BINDS */
define O_BIND_D     = 35;
define O_BIND_L     = 36;
define O_BIND_R     = 37;

define O_MBIND_U    = 38;     /* p7  TS BINDS+ (modifier held) */
define O_MBIND_D    = 39;
define O_MBIND_L    = 40;
define O_MBIND_R    = 41;

define O_BREATH     = 42;     /* p8  BREATH */
define O_BR_DLY     = 43;
define O_BR_HOLD    = 44;
define O_BR_REST    = 45;

define O_QS_ON      = 46;     /* p9  QUICKSCOPE */
define O_QS_DLY     = 47;
define O_QS_HOLD    = 48;
define O_RESCOPE    = 49;
define O_RESC_DLY   = 50;

define O_BOLT_ON    = 51;     /* p10 BOLT WORK */
define O_BOLT_DLY   = 52;
define O_RELCAN     = 53;

define O_DROP       = 54;     /* p11 MOVEMENT */
define O_JUMPS      = 55;
define O_SPRINT     = 56;
define O_YYCAN      = 57;
